MeeGo-like home (pro1x-maemo-leste patches/meego), on with GConf
/apps/osso/hildon-desktop/meego_pages: the home views, the launcher and the
task navigator in a ring, changed by swiping, without the top left buttons;
in applications, swipes from the left or right edge to the open
applications, from the top edge down to close, a tap on the top edge for
the menu. Applications without a title bar below the status area, which
lies across the top as the N9's thin status bar; the root window's
_HILDON_MEEGO_LOOK for the other parts (hildon-status-menu, libhildon); the
application menu as a list below the bar; the launcher's icons in the
N9's shape (the N9's own where its theme is installed). The status bar
also over the launcher and the task navigator. Home widgets that scroll
(_HILDON_MEEGO_SCROLLING_APPLET, the Events page) get the drags up and
down; applets begin right below the bar.
In portrait as on the N9: the pages side by side (Leste's scroll_vertical
not used with the look), the launcher with the N9's buttons (4 in a row
in portrait, 7 in landscape), the open applications in two columns below
the status bar.

